-- ===== 5) 听力 6篇/30题(audio_url 待 TTS) =====
DELETE FROM public.junior_listening_exercises WHERE publisher='fltrp' AND volume='elective4' AND unit='U3';
Tom: Yes, I really want to visit Dunhuang in the northwest of China.
Mia: Dunhuang? What is so special about it?
Tom: It has hundreds of ancient caves full of beautiful wall paintings.
Mia: That sounds amazing. How will you get there?
Tom: I''ll take the fast train and then a bus to the grottoes.
Mia: Will you climb the famous sand mountain too?
Tom: Of course. I want to watch the sunset over the desert.
Mia: Send me lots of photos when you arrive!
Tom: I promise I will.', 'Mia 问 Tom 暑假去哪儿;Tom 想去中国西北的敦煌,因为那里有数百个满是壁画的古老洞窟;他打算先坐高铁再转公交去石窟,还要爬鸣沙山看沙漠日落;Mia 让他到了多拍照片,Tom 答应了。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where does Tom want to go?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Dunhuang.","Beijing.","Shanghai.","Guangzhou."]},{"q":"Why does Tom think the place is special?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It has the biggest shopping centre.","It has ancient caves full of wall paintings.","It has a famous football team.","It is by the sea."]},{"q":"How will Tom get to the grottoes?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["By fast train and then a bus.","By plane only.","By boat across a lake.","On foot all the way."]},{"q":"What does Tom want to watch over the desert?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A football match.","The sunset.","A street market.","A boat race."]},{"q":"What does Mia ask Tom to do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Buy her a new phone.","Bring back some sand.","Send her lots of photos.","Call her every hour."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U3', 'fltrp');
They were carved out of the rock over about a thousand years.
There are more than seven hundred caves in all.
Inside, the walls are covered with colourful paintings and statues.
Today the caves are protected, and visitors come from many countries to see them.', '莫高窟坐落在敦煌城附近;历经约一千年从岩石中开凿而成;共有七百多个洞窟;洞内墙壁布满彩色壁画和雕像;如今洞窟受到保护,各国游客纷纷前来参观。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Where do the Mogao Grottoes lie?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Inside a busy seaport.","On a small island.","Next to the capital.","Near the city of Dunhuang."]},{"q":"How long did it take to carve the caves?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["About a thousand years.","About ten days.","Around fifty years.","A single winter."]},{"q":"How many caves are there in all?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Fewer than ten.","More than seven hundred.","Exactly one.","About fifty."]},{"q":"What covers the walls inside the caves?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Modern photographs.","Maps of Europe.","Colourful paintings and statues.","Glass windows."]},{"q":"Who comes to see the caves today?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only local farmers.","Nobody at all.","Only the painters.","Visitors from many countries."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U3', 'fltrp');
Visitor: Yes! They look like dancers in the sky. Who are they?
Guide: They are the Apsaras, also called the Flying Immortals.
Visitor: Their scarves seem to move as if there were a wind.
Guide: That is the skill of the old painters. They painted these during the Tang Dynasty.
Visitor: The colours are still so bright after all these years.
Guide: That is why we keep the light very low, to protect them.
Visitor: Thank you. I will never forget these wonderful paintings.', '导游让游客抬头看墙上飞舞的人物;游客觉得他们像天空中的舞者,问是谁;导游说那是飞天,又称“飞行的神仙”,绘于唐代;色彩历经多年仍鲜亮,所以洞内灯光保持很暗以保护壁画;游客说永远不会忘记这些精美的画。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does the guide ask the visitor to look at?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The flying figures on the wall.","The floor of the cave.","A book on a table.","The door behind them."]},{"q":"What are the Apsaras also called?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The Silk Traders.","The Flying Immortals.","The Desert Kings.","The Tang Soldiers."]},{"q":"When were these paintings made?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Last year.","In modern times.","During the Tang Dynasty.","Before any caves existed."]},{"q":"Why does the guide keep the light very low?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["To save electricity only.","Because the lamps are broken.","So visitors will leave quickly.","To protect the paintings."]},{"q":"How does the visitor feel about the paintings?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["She will never forget them.","She finds them boring.","She wants to touch them.","She thinks they are ugly."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U3', 'fltrp');
While cleaning a cave, he found a small room that had been closed for hundreds of years.
Inside were thousands of old papers, scrolls and paintings.
Today this room is called the Library Cave.
The papers tell us much about life on the Silk Road, but no one knows why the room was sealed.', '1900年,一位道士在敦煌有了惊人的发现;他在清理洞窟时,发现一个封闭了数百年的小室;里面藏有成千上万的古老纸卷、卷轴和画作;这个小室如今被称为藏经洞;这些文书让我们了解丝路上的生活,但无人知道它为何被封。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who made the discovery in 1900?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A foreign king.","A Taoist priest.","A young painter.","A train driver."]},{"q":"What was he doing when he found the room?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Selling tickets.","Painting a wall.","Cleaning a cave.","Riding a camel."]},{"q":"What was inside the small room?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Boxes of fresh fruit.","Modern machines.","Nothing at all.","Thousands of old papers, scrolls and paintings."]},{"q":"What do the papers tell us about?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Life on the Silk Road.","The price of gold today.","How to build trains.","The weather in Europe."]},{"q":"What is still unknown?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Where Dunhuang is.","Why the room was sealed.","Who found the room.","What was inside."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U3', 'fltrp');
Jack: Because the Silk Road passed right through it.
Lily: So traders from different lands all stopped there?
Jack: Yes, and they brought not only goods but also new ideas and art.
Lily: That must be why the cave paintings show so many cultures.
Jack: Exactly. Today the city holds a big cultural Expo every year.
Lily: I''d love to take part in it one day.
Jack: Me too. It''s a great way to learn from other countries.', 'Lily 问历史老师为何说敦煌是东西方交汇点;Jack 说因为丝绸之路正好穿城而过;各地商人都在此停留,带来货物,也带来新思想和艺术;这就是壁画展现多种文化的原因;如今城里每年举办大型文化博览会;两人都想有朝一日参加,因为这是向他国学习的好方式。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What did the teacher call Dunhuang?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["The capital of China.","A quiet fishing town.","A meeting point of East and West.","A modern factory city."]},{"q":"Why was it a meeting point?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It had the only airport.","It was beside the ocean.","It had no other towns nearby.","The Silk Road passed right through it."]},{"q":"Besides goods, what did traders bring?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["New ideas and art.","Only gold coins.","Soldiers and weapons.","Nothing else."]},{"q":"What does the city hold every year today?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A camel race only.","A big cultural Expo.","A winter snow show.","A football cup."]},{"q":"Why does Jack think the Expo is good?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It makes the city quiet.","It keeps tourists away.","It is a way to learn from other countries.","It sells cheap food."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U3', 'fltrp');
Book your ticket early, because only a few people may enter each cave every day.
Bring a hat and water, since the desert sun is very strong.
Inside the caves, please speak quietly and never touch the walls.
In this way, the wonderful paintings can be kept safe for everyone who comes after us.', '如果你打算参观敦煌的洞窟,这里有些实用建议:早点订票,因为每天每个洞窟只允许少数人进入;带上帽子和水,因为沙漠的阳光很强;在洞内请轻声说话,切勿触摸墙壁;这样,精美的壁画才能为后来的每个人妥善保存。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What should you do early?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Eat your lunch.","Climb the mountain.","Pack your camera.","Book your ticket."]},{"q":"Why should you book early?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Only a few people may enter each cave each day.","Tickets are free in the morning.","The caves close at noon.","The train is always late."]},{"q":"Why bring a hat and water?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It often rains hard.","The desert sun is very strong.","The caves are very cold.","The walk is very short."]},{"q":"What should you do inside the caves?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Shout to your friends.","Lean on the paintings.","Speak quietly and not touch the walls.","Run from cave to cave."]},{"q":"What is the purpose of this advice?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["To sell more drinks.","To make the visit longer.","To close the caves for good.","To keep the paintings safe for the future."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U3', 'fltrp');

-- ===== 6) 写作 1篇 =====
DELETE FROM public.junior_writing_prompts WHERE publisher='fltrp' AND volume='elective4' AND unit='U3';

Great to hear that you''re coming to China! If you want both fun and culture, I''d strongly recommend Dunhuang in the northwest. Although it sits on the edge of the desert, it is one of the richest cultural cities in the country. What makes it special is the Mogao Grottoes, where hundreds of ancient caves are covered with beautiful wall paintings. You should go because the murals show how East once met West along the Silk Road. Visit in the early morning so that you can also watch the sunrise over the sand mountain. You''ll love it!

Yours,
Li Hua', '【15 分制】A 档(13-15):五要素齐全、组织有条理、语言准确多样;B 档(10-12):要点较全、少量错误;C 档(7-9):要点偏少、句型简单;D 档(0-6):内容不完整、错误多。', '["If you want both fun and culture, I''d strongly recommend Dunhuang in the northwest.","Although it sits on the edge of the desert, it is one of the richest cultural cities in the country.","You should go because the murals show how East once met West along the Silk Road.","Visit in the early morning so that you can also watch the sunrise over the sand mountain."]'::jsonb, '[{"wrong":"Although it sits in the desert, but it is rich in culture.","correct":"Although it sits in the desert, it is rich in culture.","note":"although 与 but 不能同时出现在一句中。"},{"wrong":"Go early so that you can watching the sunrise.","correct":"Go early so that you can watch the sunrise.","note":"情态动词 can 后接动词原形。"},{"wrong":"I recommend Dunhuang because of it has many caves.","correct":"I recommend Dunhuang because it has many caves.","note":"because 接句子,because of 接名词/短语,不可混用。"}]'::jsonb, '【推荐信结构】
第1句 问候:Great to hear that you''re coming to China!
第2句 推荐:If you want …, I''d strongly recommend …
第3-4句 特别之处 + 理由:What makes it special is … You should go because …
第5句 建议/结尾:Visit early so that … You''ll love it!', 2, 'elective4', 'U3', 'fltrp');

